{"name":"Hot Pink Fusion","hex":"#fe69b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Hote."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to heat and conditions which produce it.\n Having or giving off a high temperature.","Having or giving off a high temperature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"fusion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of merging separate things, or the result thereof.\n\n A nuclear reaction in which nuclei combine to form more massive nuclei with the concomitant release of energy. \n A style of music that blends disparate genres; especially different types of jazz and reggae.\nA style of cooking that combines ingredients and techniques from different countries or cultures\nThe act of melting or liquefying something by heating it.\n\n The result of the hybridation of two genes which originally coded for separate proteins.\n The process by which two distinct lipid bilayers merge their hydrophobic core, resulting in one interconnected structure.\n The act of two characters merging into one, typically more powerful, being; or the merged being itself.","A nuclear reaction in which nuclei combine to form more massive nuclei with the concomitant release of energy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To combine; to fuse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fusion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink colors are usually light or desaturated shades of reds, roses, and magentas which are created on computer and television screens using the RGB color model and in printing with the CMYK color model. As such, it is an arbitrary classification of color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Color_icon_pink_v2.svg/330px-Color_icon_pink_v2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_pink","wikidata":"Q19847189"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Globe_amaranth.jpg/500px-Globe_amaranth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Globe_amaranth.jpg/500px-Globe_amaranth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink globe amaranth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlobe_amaranth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Row_of_sakura%2C_Asuwa_River%2C_Fukui.jpg/500px-Row_of_sakura%2C_Asuwa_River%2C_Fukui.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Row_of_sakura%2C_Asuwa_River%2C_Fukui.jpg/1280px-Row_of_sakura%2C_Asuwa_River%2C_Fukui.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Row_of_sakura%2C_Asuwa_River%2C_Fukui.jpg/500px-Row_of_sakura%2